	(text "OPTIONAL 0603 PADS C1-C6 (not populated, DNP): the PCM5100A charge pump and supply decoupling at the chip\n(C1-C3 on the back, across the pin 1-5 tracks; C4-C6 on the front, across the pin 8/9 and 18-20 tracks).\nLeave them EMPTY on PicoGUS: the main board already has these parts (C36, C16, C17, C18, C13/C15) next to the DIP-20.\nFit them only if the adapter is used on a board without them (then also tie CPGND, AGND and DGND together)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 105.41 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "55db9a36-ebd7-51d0-8246-0700e83cefc8")
	)
	(text "TSSOP-20 -> DIP-20 300 mil adapter, PicoGUS THT v1.3.2. Use: U9 (PCM5100A) on PicoGUS THT v1.3.2.\nMapping: TSSOP pin n -> DIP pin n for every pin (net names Pn_<pin name>); nothing else in the signal path.\nBoard: 10.16 x 25.40 mm, 1 mm chamfer at the pin-1 corner = the body outline of the main-board footprint\nDIP-20_W7.62mm_TSSOP-20_Adapter (it fits that courtyard).\nAssembly: solder the TSSOP first. Then fit two 1x10 round machined pin strips from the BOTTOM (insulator under\nthe board), solder them on the top and cut the tails flush. J1 holes 0.85 mm. The round 0.47 mm pins fit\nmachined DIP sockets (On Shore SA203000) and the 1.0 mm main-board holes.\nThe 0.85 mm holes take round machined pins only (Preci-Dip 350: 0.64 mm tail; Mill-Max 350: 0.46 mm tail)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 53.34 118.11 0)
